# Briefing Note SOP
<!-- [W] Created 13-Apr-26. Automatic capture of ESA/DD research briefings as tagged Stock Notes pages. -->
<!-- Referenced by: RESEARCHER role file (SKILL.md) -->

## Purpose

When Richard briefs Watson on ESA or DD research for a stock, Watson **automatically** saves a comprehensive, synthesised note of the briefing exchange to the Stock Notes DB in Notion. This creates a written record of Richard's thinking, priorities, hypotheses, and agreed research direction at the point of briefing — before any research execution begins.

---

## When to Trigger

**Automatic — no permission asked.**

| Stage | Trigger? | Rationale |
|-------|----------|-----------|
| **ESA** | **YES** | Briefing captures Richard's priors, hypotheses, and research direction at a decision point (IG → ESA promotion) |
| **DD (P1 and RO)** | **YES** | Briefing captures deepening focus, key questions, and what needs resolving |
| **IG** | No | IG is mechanical (BD + CF prompts). No substantive briefing to capture |
| **Triaging** | No | Triaging uses standardised checklists. No substantive briefing to capture |
| **Monitoring / Info Flow** | No | Standing instructions, not stock-specific briefings |

**Trigger condition:** Richard provides a stock-specific research brief that includes context, direction, hypotheses, key questions, or focus areas for ESA or DD work. Watson recognises this as a briefing and captures it.

---

## Format: Synthesised Briefing Memo (Option B)

The note is a **synthesised memo** — NOT a verbatim Q&A log. Watson restructures the briefing conversation into a clean, topically-organised document. The goal is a note Richard can skim later and immediately recall what he was thinking and what was agreed.

### Required Sections

Every briefing note must include the following sections (use H2 headers). Skip a section only if the briefing genuinely contained nothing relevant to it.

#### 1. `## Context & Stage Transition`
Why this stock is progressing to ESA/DD now. What triggered the promotion. Where it sits in the pipeline. What IG/prior work revealed.

#### 2. `## Richard's Priors & Hypotheses`
What Richard already believes about this stock. His working thesis. Initial pattern recognition (archetype, setup type). Conviction level. What excited him or raised flags at IG stage.

#### 3. `## Key Questions for {Stage}`
The specific questions the ESA/DD research needs to answer. Prioritised. These become the research agenda.

#### 4. `## Focus Areas & Angles`
Specific dimensions Richard wants emphasised. Which parts of the business matter most. Which drivers to investigate. Any thematic overlays (e.g., Iran risk, regulatory change, sector dynamics).

#### 5. `## Known Risks & Concerns`
What Richard is worried about. Red flags from IG. Things that could kill the case. "False friend" signals.

#### 6. `## Agreed Research Plan`
Watson's synthesised plan: which prompts to run, which KQs to research, sequencing, any special instructions. This is Watson's analysis of the brief — what needs to happen and in what order.

#### 7. `## Constraints & Context`
Time pressure, market context (risk-on/off), portfolio context (existing exposure, correlated positions), any external factors shaping the research priority.

### Optional Sections (include when relevant)

- `## Comparable Cases / Archetypes` — If Richard references prior stocks, patterns, or archetypes during the briefing
- `## Financial Priors` — If Richard mentions specific financial expectations (growth rates, margins, multiples)
- `## Management / Operator Assessment` — If Richard has views on management quality from IG

